#EXTINF:-1 group-title="Sciences - Environment" tvg-id="202394197" tvg-name="The planet's jet streams are being affected by rising temperatures in the Arctic. These streams are part of a wind system that circulates at high altitude around the Earth‚ and they have an influence on extreme weather events. Changes in them are bad news for life on Earth.<br/>From 25.07.2023 05:00" tvg-country="Germany" tvg-language="English" channel-id="ARTE.EN",Winds of Change - How Climate Change Makes Storms Worse (Originalversion mit Untertitel) (25.07.2023)
